  "id": "RLSA-2026:82882",
  "title": "Important: hplip security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-16 12:05:26"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-23 00:16:47"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The hplip packages contain the Hewlett-Packard Linux Imaging and Printing Project (HPLIP), which provides drivers for Hewlett-Packard printers and multi-function peripherals.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* hplip: HP Linux Imaging and Printing Software - Use of DSA Key (CVE-2025-43023)\n\n* hplip: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities enabling local code execution and privilege escalation (CVE-2026-91099)\n\n* hplip: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities allow remote code execution and privilege escalation (CVE-2026-91098)\n\n* hplip: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities enable remote code execution and privilege escalation (CVE-2026-91097)\n\n* hplip: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities leading to remote code execution, privilege escalation, and denial of service (CVE-2026-91103)\n\n* hplip: heap-based buffer overflow can lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-91106)\n\n* hplip: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities allow remote code execution, privilege escalation, and denial of service. (CVE-2026-91100)\n\n* hplip: HPLIP: Remote Code Execution and Privilege Escalation Vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-91101)\n\n* hplip: heap-based buffer overflow can lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-91104)\n\n* hplip: HPLIP: Remote code execution and privilege escalation vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-91105)\n\n* HPLIP: HPLIP: Multiple vulnerabilities could lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-91102)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* [IMAGE-MODE] missing /var/lib/hp on image-mode (JIRA:Rocky Linux-257310)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
